detailed_feedback: "The candidate shows promising technical foundations with their computer science education and research experience. Their Python skills, while present, are primarily focused on machine learning rather than backend development. The 2 years of total experience, mostly in different domains, falls significantly short of the 7+ years required for this senior role.\n\nTheir GitHub profile shows limited public activity and no relevant backend API projects. While they demonstrate good practices with Git version control, there's no evidence of experience with the FastAPI ecosystem or any of its core components (Starlette, Pydantic, asyncio).\n\nThe infrastructure automation experience from Deutsche Börse suggests technical adaptability, but the lack of specific backend development experience and Docker knowledge represents significant skill gaps for this position."
hiring_manager_notes: "This candidate is too junior for the current senior backend developer position. While they show strong technical potential and learning ability, they lack both the years of experience and specific technical expertise required for framework maintenance and senior-level responsibilities.\n\nRecommend keeping their profile on file for future junior backend developer positions. Their strong computer science foundation and demonstrated ability to work with complex systems (ML research, infrastructure automation) suggests good potential for growth in backend development with proper mentoring.\n\nIf proceeding with other candidates, suggest providing constructive feedback focusing on the experience gap and encouraging them to gain hands-on experience with FastAPI and backend API development through personal projects or junior roles."